# Shared Packages Rules

## Package Structure

Each package domain follows:

```
src/packages/entities/{domain}/
├── {domain}.schema.ts   # Zod validation schemas
├── {domain}.dto.ts      # TypeScript interfaces/types
└── index.ts             # Re-exports
```

## Zod Schema Conventions

- Define schemas using Zod v4 syntax
- Use `z.object()` for request/response shapes
- Export inferred types: `export type CreateDto = z.infer<typeof CreateSchema>`
- Use `.strict()` to strip unknown fields
- Reuse schema fragments with `z.intersection()` or spread

## DTO Conventions

- DTO files contain ONLY TypeScript types/interfaces
- Do NOT duplicate Zod schema definitions in DTOs
- Use `z.infer<typeof X>` for type derivation
- Export domain interfaces for service/repository return types

## Decorators

- `@Public()` - skip JWT auth for public endpoints
- `@Admin()` - require admin role for protected endpoints
- `@User()` - extract user from request in controller params
- `@ApiResponse()` - standardize Swagger response docs

## Guards

- `JwtAuthGuard` - global guard applied via `APP_GUARD`
- `AdminRoleGuard` - role-based access for admin routes
- Guards should never contain business logic

## Pipes

- `ZodValidationPipe` - validate request bodies against Zod schemas
- Always pass schema as constructor arg: `new ZodValidationPipe(Schema)`
- Pipe handles transformation + error formatting

## Interceptors

- `ResponseInterceptor` - wraps all responses in standard format
- `ErrorInterceptor` - catches and formats errors
- `LoggerInterceptor` - logs request/response info
- Order in main.ts: Logger → Response → Error

## Filters

- `HttpExceptionFilter` - global exception handler
- Formats error responses consistently
- Handles validation errors, HTTP exceptions, unexpected errors
